# Normalize line endings to LF in the repo. Shell scripts, Python and workflow
# YAML must be LF to run on Linux CI / in consumers, regardless of a contributor's
# core.autocrlf. (See the global convention: normalize anything executed on Linux.)
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary

# Changelogs are append-only bullet lists that every PR edits at the same spot
# (top of "## [Unreleased]"), so parallel PRs conflict on identical-location adds.
# `union` is a BUILT-IN git merge driver (no local config, so GitHub honors it too):
# on conflict it keeps BOTH sides' lines instead of stopping. Order isn't guaranteed
# and identical lines can dupe — both tidied when a release is cut — but the conflict
# class disappears. Applies to any repo that vendors this file.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
